Anzu is a small, light bird-like man (a tengu) with feathers and a beak, able to fly on his own wings, and a member of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]]. He shares leadership of the Party with [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] since its founder [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Illmari Vaino|Illmari]] went missing. He is well-studied in occult and religious matters and is the Party's reader of magic: he identifies what they find, names the creatures they meet, and works out their riddles. He keeps the raven [[People/Othello|Othello]], a pet-shop bird he rewired to carry the memories of the first Othello, killed by fire beneath [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]], and carries a staff of light wood he made himself, with a perch for Othello. His head runs a few degrees hotter than the rest of him, which his friends noticed.

He comes from [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]], where his family, the [[People/Qureshi|Qureshis]], are a noble line that funds [[Org/Belvedere/index|Belvedere]]. He is one of three triplets: his brother [[People/Aguirzu|Aguirzu]] is in good standing, and his sister [[People/Galzu|Galzu]] went missing after months spent with the [[Org/Singers of the Herald's Star|Singers of the Herald's Star]].

Born with his family's psychic gift, he could not reach it until he heard the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]], and the song is the center of his work. He speaks in his own mind to a Vocalist he takes for the source of the song. He has wired the [[Phenomena/Sentience Distributor|sentience distributor]] to his own mind, and the anchor it left in him is no longer the pure Voidsong but a hybrid of it and the harmony the true kin of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] carry under their sleep. He means to tune the distributor to cancel the parts where the Herald Song and the Voidsong differ, which needs a living singer of the Herald Song taken alive.

He holds that his sister [[People/Galzu|Galzu]] was drawn into the [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]]'s work against her will. The [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Machine God|Machine God]] found her in Neweth, the town around the heart [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Tally|Tally]], and Anzu found her there himself at the dead Heart, working to wake it. He and the others beat her down and took her alive, and he entered her mind to break the god's hold, only to find her defenses past him. She is held now in a suspension chamber at [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Lifeline|Lifeline]], and he has a few weeks to move the strider before she grows beyond his reach.

He was the only survivor of the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]], and killed the half-giant [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] and the gang's leader [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]]. He travels with [[People/Johnny|Johnny Skyfall]], [[People/Benny|Benny]], [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] and [[People/Sir Arctos|Sir Arctos]], and unlike them carries no mark of [[Aut]].

In his own head he carries a trace of the [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]]'s song, and the Voidsong crowds it out; the two harmonies work against each other. He put this to use on [[People/Egan Arithmites|Egan]], whose mind he entered with the others to study the Herald song's hold there, and he drove the Voidsong into Egan's head in place of it, the first time the song has passed from one listener to another.
